verbatim_audit:
  line_audition: "ok listened to opener 4 & 5. both are good. But 5, at the end, 'writing them' it seemed to have a bit of a robotic feel to it." — #4 cleared without defect call; #5 carried flagged robotic-tail defect on kicker; unflawed #4 ships.
  janet_character_flag: "Janet is a bit more mature, not old. But not young either. Tough as nails, doesn't take shit from anyone, especially Dash. She loves him, just doesn't take shit from him. I think her voice needs to be toughened up - in a matriach kinda way." — original Sarah voice was too "reassuring" for Janet's character; triggered voice iteration.
  voice_iteration_v2_matilda: "Matilda could work. But let's try some from our scout." — direction-right but escalate to Shared Library scout.
  voice_iteration_v3_sloane: "ooooohhhhh I likey. Let's do one more, but yeah that's good." — winning timbre; one more A/B for diagnostic confidence.
  voice_iteration_v4_kristen: "Kirsten is good, really good. But Sloane is our gal." — A/B confirms Sloane.
phase_4_carry_forward:
  candidate_5_defect: "robotic feel on trailing 'writing them' phrase — Phase 4 recovery path: [exhale] tag swap OR lower stability + bump style OR shorten kicker; OR re-render with Sloane + matriarch-tuned (free attempt since the matriarch-tuned profile already cleared the kicker defect on #4)"
  janet_voice_dna_brief: "mature but not old; tough as nails; doesn't take shit from anyone, especially Dash; loves him, just doesn't take shit from him. Malory-archetype scotch-and-cigarettes matriarch. Sloane + matriarch-tuned settings is the locked recipe."
  janet_voice_reusability: "Sloane + matriarch-tuned is now the canonical Janet voice for any future Janet dialogue Phase 4 might author beyond the cold-open; no re-pick required."
phase_6_provisional: Y — Phase 6 N=6 cold-decode panel re-validates per cross-phase ADR #21 (single-reader fallback gate is provisional until Phase 6).
